READ_FILE infra/compose/README.md
1:# R01 local and isolated deployment
2:
3:Compose 2.24.4 or later is required for `include`, `!override` and `!reset`.
4:Supply configuration through the environment or a private `--env-file` outside
5:the repository. Set `COMPOSE_DISABLE_ENV_FILE=1` to prevent implicit `.env` loading.
6:`config/dev.env.example` lists names only: credentials, URLs, image references
7:and exclusive host ports must be supplied explicitly. Do not run `compose config`
8:into a shared log: its output includes interpolated credentials.
9:
10:Choose an explicit `dianzi-dev-<name>` project. `core` starts PostgreSQL and
11:authenticated Redis; `search` adds OpenSearch with its security plugin enabled.
12:`app`, `worker`, `scheduler` and `frontend` select the actual runtime entrypoints
13:and their required services. Search is optional; when selected, supply its URL.
14:`COMPOSE_DATABASE_URL`, `COMPOSE_REDIS_URL` and `COMPOSE_ALLOWED_ORIGINS` are
15:deployment inputs: Compose maps them to the application variable names inside
16:containers. They do not configure a pytest or management process on the host.
17:The backend application URLs use `postgres:5432`, `redis:6379` and, when selected,
18:the configured search endpoint inside the private network. Browser URLs use the
19:published localhost ports. `ALLOWED_ORIGINS` must be exact JSON origins.
20:
21:The Dockerfiles and Compose build arguments pin the actually pulled official
22:Python 3.12, uv 0.10.9 and Node 24 RepoDigests. Dockerfiles
23:install the checked-in locks, copy only required source/config files and use
24:nonroot application users. The CI service job does not build or start application images.
25:
26:```powershell
27:docker compose --project-name dianzi-dev-myname -f infra/compose/compose.yaml --profile core --profile search up -d --wait
28:docker compose --project-name dianzi-dev-myname -f infra/compose/compose.yaml --profile app --profile worker --profile scheduler --profile frontend up -d --build
29:docker compose --project-name dianzi-dev-myname -f infra/compose/compose.yaml --profile core --profile search --profile app --profile worker --profile scheduler --profile frontend down
30:```
31:
32:`down` preserves all named volumes. API readiness verifies the real dependency
33:connections and installed migration revision. Starting the application does not
34:migrate a database or create accounts. Apply migrations and create users through
35:the explicit management CLI after checking the target identity. Scheduler health
36:checks beat process liveness; it is not evidence that a business task completed.
37:
38:The bounded data-service allocation is PostgreSQL 512 MiB/0.4 CPU/128 PIDs,
39:Redis 128 MiB/0.1 CPU/64 PIDs and OpenSearch 2 GiB/0.5 CPU/256 PIDs (512 MiB heap,
40:no mmap). Application services add 1.125 GiB/0.85 CPU. Persistent storage size
41:depends on source bytes and retained versions; no sustained capacity result is
42:claimed. The private network has no outbound route; external business traffic
43:requires the separately authorized gateway configuration.
44:
45:## Test projects
46:
47:`compose.test.yaml` includes the base and replaces the development database and
48:ports. The database is `test_dianzi_<DIANZI_TEST_RUN_ID>`; supply a dedicated
49:`TEST_POSTGRES_USER`, random URL-safe test credentials and exclusive test ports.
50:The application URLs in this overlay use the container service names. The
51:`TEST_DATABASE_URL`, `TEST_REDIS_URL`, `TEST_OPENSEARCH_URL` consumed by host-side
52:tests use loopback and the published exclusive ports.
53:
54:Set `DIANZI_TEST_COMPOSE_PROJECT=dianzi-test-<DIANZI_TEST_RUN_ID>` and
55:`DIANZI_TEST_COMPOSE_FILE` to the existing test entry file. The shared quality
56:entrypoint rejects a nonisolated PostgreSQL DSN before running tests or Compose.
57:Missing resources fail with `blocked`; no test resource is substituted or skipped.
58:
59:`compose.test.host.yaml` is only for the specifically authorized Linux daemon
60:with bridge networking disabled. It clears published ports and bridge networks;
61:PostgreSQL, Redis, OpenSearch HTTP/transport, API and frontend bind internally to
62:127.0.0.1 on exclusive configured ports. It also changes application URLs to the
63:host-side loopback test URLs. It must not be used as a production deployment.
64:OpenSearch security is disabled only in explicit localhost test overlays.
65:
66:The R01-infra run uses project `dianzi-test-r01_infra_20261015`, PostgreSQL 25436,
67:Redis 26383, OpenSearch 29201/29301. The private random connection configuration
68:is root-only outside this repository. The authorized daemon expires at
69:2026-10-17T21:49:15+08:00; this package does not extend it or change host limits.
